    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to present to the market this charming two-bedroom end-of-terrace home, ideally positioned on Ennel Avenue in the ever-popular Artane area of Dublin 5. Offering excellent potential for both first-time buyers and those looking to put their own stamp on a property, this well-proportioned home benefits from off-street parking to the front and a particularly attractive south-east facing rear garden.\n\nThe accommodation is laid out over two levels and briefly comprises an entrance hallway, living room, kitchen, dining room, reception room and utility area at ground floor level. Upstairs there are two well-proportioned bedrooms and a family bathroom. The property offers generous living accommodation and, as an end-of-terrace home, enjoys the added benefit of increased privacy and natural light.\n\nUpon entering, the welcoming hallway provides access to the principal reception areas. The living room is a comfortable space to relax, while the kitchen and dining room provide a practical setting for everyday family living and entertaining. A further reception room offers excellent versatility and could be utilised as a family room, home office, playroom or additional living space. The utility area provides useful additional storage and household facilities.\n\nUpstairs, there are two bedrooms, both offering good proportions and ample scope for storage, together with the family bathroom. The accommodation provides a comfortable layout while also offering the new owner an opportunity to modernise and personalise the property to their own taste.\n\nTo the front, there is valuable off-street parking, while to the rear lies the real highlight of the property — a private south-east facing garden. Enjoying excellent natural light, the rear garden provides a wonderful outdoor space for relaxing, entertaining and enjoying the sunshine throughout the day.\n\nThe location is superb, with a host of amenities close by including shops, schools, sports and recreational facilities, while the nearby areas of Artane, Coolock, Donaghmede and Killester provide an excellent choice of cafés, restaurants and shopping facilities. The property is also well served by public transport, providing convenient access to Dublin City Centre and surrounding areas.\n\nOverall, 16 Ennel Avenue represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a well-located two-bedroom end-of-terrace home with off-street parking and a superb south-east facing rear garden. While requiring some modernisation, the property offers excellent potential and will appeal to a wide range of buyers seeking a home in this established and convenient Dublin 5 location.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to appreciate the potential and location of this fine home."
      },
